hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"12","Umar bin Abdul Aziz (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates: When Muawiyah bin Abu Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him) returned from Hajj and arrived in Madinah, Saeed bin Aas stood up to welcome him. Upon this, Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Your brother has more understanding of religion than you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Whoever likes that, when he comes, people stand up for him, Allah will build a house for him in Hell.'"""
